Code ported into this repository, with modifications
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

overlay/mods/qsa-kv-fp8/run.sh (fp8_e4m3 KV cache on the QSA attention path) has two
independent, later, public counterparts that reach the same four integration points:

  vllm-project/vllm issue #54426, "[RFC] Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: fp8_e4m3 KV cache on the
  QSA path — working patch, one machine, looking for corroboration", by Nanetnounou,
  opened 2026-08-30, measured on a GB10 / sm_121 like ours.
  vllm-project/vllm PR #54846, "[Model] Qwen4Exp: fp8_e4m3 and nvfp4 KV cache on the
  QSA path", by andreasgru, opened 2026-09-01. Apache License 2.0.

Our script was written and validated on 2026-08-28 (measurement on the FP8 build, not in
results/), before either was opened, and without knowledge of them. We became aware of both
on 2026-09-04 and read them as independent corroboration (pool x1.79 on #54426, x1.889 on
#54846, against our x1.84). We claim independence, not priority: three people wrote against
the same six refusals in the same file and reached the same conclusions because the code
leaves little room for others. No line was copied in any direction. If #54846 merges, this script becomes unnecessary on that engine and should
be dropped, not maintained. The one earlier vLLM change our script does pattern itself
on, and says so inline, is PR #47665 (read-time cast that folds to a no-op on bf16
caches).

